# Text files are stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout inherits core.autocrlf=true (the Git for
# Windows default, and the windows-latest runner default) and every file lands
# as CRLF. gofmt prints LF, so it then reports *every* Go file as unformatted:
# the CI build-windows job failed on its formatting gate from its very first
# run while build and vet — both CRLF-tolerant — passed. Pinning the checkout
# EOL here fixes the cause instead of loosening the gate.
* text=auto eol=lf
